body:
@ChethanaMallisetty21 thanks for your interest.

We are currently having quite some traffic in the test files due to #3408 , but help is welcome. In order to minimize the amount of conflicts, and coordinate smoothly, would you be up for starting with just `test_batch.py` and `test_session.py`?

Please note the latest edit I made to the issue. There are two main ways of solving the need for `get_mocked_x`: one of them is using the `mock_responses` decorator that allows the test to replicate what would happen when using the actual service, and the other one is using a fake backend (which equates to using local mode). Using a fake backend is preferred as it has less complexity, and the decision is on a per-test basis: understanding the goal of the test, and deciding based on that.
